# Text is stored and checked out as LF everywhere. Prettier's endOfLine default is
# "lf", so without this a Windows clone (core.autocrlf=true) gets CRLF working
# copies and `pnpm format:check` fails on files the contributor never touched.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Patch data is binary and must never be line-ending converted. Git's own
# detection looks for a NUL byte early in the file, which a short SysEx dump need
# not have - a misdetected voice bank would be silently corrupted on checkout.
*.syx binary
*.SYX binary
*.mx binary
*.MX binary
*.Dx7Voice binary
*.dx7voice binary
*.sqlite3 binary

*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.wav binary
*.mid binary
